    {
      "id": "heidemarie-linked-and-quietus",
      "title": {
        "en": "Heidemarie Linked and Quietus"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_30093_srt4",
              "name": "Sword Rain",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30093_uni1",
              "name": "Hero to All",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30093_uni4",
              "name": "Effulgent Compression",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Linked is Hide's main Mechanic\nIf Cards are Linked together that means\nIf one of the Linked cards are used, the rest are discarded\nThe discard happens on cast, not on card resolution\nSo you cannot use a Linked card, then try to affect another Linked card\nThis does make Nia a bit more unfortunate with Hero to All"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Effulgent Blades Compression and Release"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_30093_srt4",
              "name": "Sword Rain",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30093_uni3",
              "name": "Effulgent Expansion",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30093_uni4",
              "name": "Effulgent Compression",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Effulgent Blades are Heide's main created cards\nThey can be discarded for Extra Attack Damage\nBut the main fact about them is how they infinitly stack inside your Discard Pile\nWhile not bricking and filling your draw pile reshuffles\nEffulgent Compression once turned into Release becomes a MASSIVE NUKE\nThat scales based on the amount of Effulgent Blades you have in discard pile"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
